From: Codex hardware porting
Subject: [PATCH] pwm: mediatek: accept C-unit MT69xx PWM compatible

The C-unit DT uses the vendor spelling "mediatek,mt69xx-pwm". The existing
6.18 MT6990 data describes the same seven-channel block (base 0x80, stride
0x40); add the DT compatible alias without changing the register layout.

--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-mediatek.c
@@ -542,6 +542,7 @@
 static const struct of_device_id pwm_mediatek_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt2712-pwm", .data = &mt2712_pwm_data },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6795-pwm", .data = &mt6795_pwm_data },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6990-pwm", .data = &mt6990_pwm_data },
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt69xx-pwm", .data = &mt6990_pwm_data },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6991-pwm", .data = &mt6991_pwm_data },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt7622-pwm", .data = &mt7622_pwm_data },
---
2.39.5
